IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Class Licence) (Amendment) Notification 2012 (S 70/2012), made under ss 9 and 11 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-class-licence-amendment-notification-2012/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S70-2012.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited). Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- First published 23 February 2012 at 5.00 pm; "shall come into operation on 23rd February 2012" (paragraph 1).
-- It inserts paragraph 2A (Internet content filtering by Internet Access Service Providers) in the Schedule to N 1 and amends paragraph 15(f) and (g). Paragraph 2A was replaced by S 674/2016 from 28 December 2016.

§ `Paragraph 2: the Schedule amended`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 23rd February 2012 at 5.00 pm.
-- src:20 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Broadcasting (Class Licence)
-- src:21 | (Amendment) Notification 2012 and shall come into operation on
-- src:22 | 23rd February 2012.
@ref S 70/2012 publication line and para 1 (commencement) (src:3-22)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 70/2012 the amendments are in operation on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 23 2 2012)

-- src:27 | (a) by inserting, immediately after paragraph 2, the following
-- src:28 | paragraph:
-- src:29 | ‘‘2A.—(1) An Internet Service Provider who is an Internet Access
-- src:30 | Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications
-- src:31 | Act (Cap. 323) (referred to in this paragraph as an Internet Access
-- src:32 | Service Provider) shall —
-- src:33 | (a) upon receiving, on or after 23rd February 2012, any request by
-- src:34 | any of its relevant subscribers, offer to provide that relevant
-- src:35 | subscriber Internet content filtering arrangements;
-- src:36 | (b) inform any prospective relevant subscriber in Singapore of
-- src:37 | the availability of Internet content filtering arrangements
-- src:38 | before providing, on or after 23rd February 2012, to the
-- src:39 | prospective relevant subscriber first access to the Internet;
-- src:40 | (c) inform a relevant subscriber of the availability of Internet
-- src:41 | content filtering arrangements before renewing, on or after
-- src:42 | 23rd February 2012, the subscription of that relevant
-- src:43 | subscriber; and
-- src:44 | (d) for the duration of the relevant subscriber’s subscription,
-- src:45 | provide reasonable technical support to the relevant
-- src:46 | S 70/2012 2
-- src:48 | subscriber with respect to the provision of Internet content
-- src:49 | filtering arrangements.
-- src:50 | (2) If the Authority is satisfied that content in a programme on
-- src:51 | the World Wide Web is undesirable, harmful or obscene, and the
-- src:52 | Authority gives to an Internet Access Service Provider written notice
-- src:53 | that end-users should be prevented from accessing that content on the
-- src:54 | Internet, the Internet Access Service Provider shall take all
-- src:55 | reasonable steps to modify, or to enable the relevant subscribers to
-- src:56 | modify, the Internet content filtering arrangements to prevent such
-- src:57 | end-users from accessing that content.
-- src:58 | (3) In this paragraph —
-- src:59 | ‘‘relevant subscriber’’ means a person in Singapore who —
-- src:60 | (a) subscribes to any computer online service that enables
-- src:61 | the person to obtain through any telecommunication
-- src:62 | line access to the Internet at a private residence,
-- src:63 | whether or not owned by the relevant subscriber; or
-- src:64 | (b) subscribes, on or after 30th June 2012, to any computer
-- src:65 | online service (excluding the excepted services) that
-- src:66 | enables the person to obtain access to the Internet
-- src:67 | through radio-communication;
@ref S 70/2012 para 2(a): Schedule para 2A(1) to (3)(a) (Internet content filtering arrangements; "relevant subscriber") (src:27-67)
GIVEN `the person subscribes to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through a telecommunication line at a private residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subscribes on or after 30 June 2012 to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is an excepted service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 70/2012 N 1 Schedule para 2A(3) the person is a relevant subscriber` MEANS
    `the person subscribes to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through a telecommunication line at a private residence` OR (`the person subscribes on or after 30 June 2012 to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through radio-communication` AND (NOT `the service is an excepted service`))

GIVEN `the provider is an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider offered filtering arrangements on a request on or after 23 February 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider told each prospective subscriber of the availability of filtering arrangements before first providing access on or after 23 February 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider told each subscriber of the availability of filtering arrangements before renewing on or after 23 February 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider gave reasonable technical support for the duration of the subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 70/2012 N 1 Schedule para 2A(1) the provider has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `the provider is an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act`) OR (`the provider offered filtering arrangements on a request on or after 23 February 2012` AND `the provider told each prospective subscriber of the availability of filtering arrangements before first providing access on or after 23 February 2012` AND `the provider told each subscriber of the availability of filtering arrangements before renewing on or after 23 February 2012` AND `the provider gave reasonable technical support for the duration of the subscription`)

GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that content in a programme on the World Wide Web is undesirable, harmful or obscene and gave written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider took all reasonable steps to modify, or to enable the relevant subscribers to modify, the filtering arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 70/2012 N 1 Schedule para 2A(2) the provider has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority is satisfied that content in a programme on the World Wide Web is undesirable, harmful or obscene and gave written notice`) OR `the provider took all reasonable steps to modify, or to enable the relevant subscribers to modify, the filtering arrangements`

-- S 70/2012 para 2(b) (deposit lines 91-92) deletes the words "the censorship section of" in Schedule para 15(f): a wording change to a paragraph the lawplain text does not serve; no rule is stated here.

-- S 70/2012 para 2(c) (deposit lines 95-102) replaces the film wording in Schedule para 15(g) with "approved for exhibition under the Films Act (Cap. 107) or exempted from the provisions of that Act or to which that Act does not apply are broadcast": a wording change to a paragraph the lawplain text does not serve; no rule is stated here.
